:'''Hyacine:''' You'd move in perfect harmony with the rivers and seas of this world.
:'''Dan Heng:''' But we can't stay. (Trailblazer) and I... we have people waiting for us, a home calling us back.
:'''Hyacine:''' The Astral Express, isn't it?
:'''Hyacine:''' March 7th, the one you always mention... I'd like to meet her someday.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm sure the two of you would get along wonderfully.
:I'm sure the two of you would get along wonderfully.
:'''Hyacine:''' I can almost see the three of you traveling together, laughing and sharing moments.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And you, Hyacine? Do you not feel sadness?
:And you, Hyacine? Do you not feel sadness?
:'''Hyacine:''' Of course, I do. A sharp, aching sadness... I feel every bit of it.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Why hide it? No one here would mock you for showing true vulnerability.
:'''Hyacine:''' As a healer from the Twilight Courtyard, Dan Heng, it's my duty to stay composed in front of those suffering from illness. A sorrowful expression would only add to their burden.
:'''Hyacine:''' The world I love is the one suffering now. How could I face it with a frown?
:'''(Trailblazer):''' ...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Farewell, Hyacinthia.
:Farewell, Hyacinthia.
